VeridianOS: WaylandPipeWriterHelper: test EWOULDBLOCK only where it differs from EAGAIN

GCC reported logical 'or' of equal expressions [-Wlogical-op] at
src/systemclipboard/waylandpipewriterhelper.cpp:32: on Linux (glibc and
musl) EWOULDBLOCK is defined as EAGAIN, so
"errno == EAGAIN || errno == EWOULDBLOCK" compares the same value twice.
POSIX allows the two to differ, so the second test is kept, compiled only
where EWOULDBLOCK != EAGAIN. No behaviour change on any platform.

diff -ru a/src/systemclipboard/waylandpipewriterhelper.cpp b/src/systemclipboard/waylandpipewriterhelper.cpp
--- a/src/systemclipboard/waylandpipewriterhelper.cpp	2026-10-08 17:31:21.141587006 -0400
+++ b/src/systemclipboard/waylandpipewriterhelper.cpp	2026-10-08 17:31:21.251160775 -0400
@@ -29,7 +29,12 @@
                 offset += n;
                 continue;
             } else if (n < 0) {
-                if (errno == EAGAIN || errno == EWOULDBLOCK)
+                // EWOULDBLOCK may be EAGAIN (it is on Linux); only test it separately where it differs.
+                if (errno == EAGAIN
+#if EWOULDBLOCK != EAGAIN
+                    || errno == EWOULDBLOCK
+#endif
+                )
                     continue;
                 if (errno == EPIPE)
                     return SafeWriteResult::Closed;
